            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Nước",
            "review_text": "conscienciouseater\nAsia, Peru2982 contributions\n0\nYou pay for beautiful ambience and great attention to details\nAug 2026 • Friends\nOne of classier Vietnamese restaurants in Saigon, conveniently located in the Thảo Điền area. Beautifully decorated interior with a pleasant garden as well. The food is not exceptional or creative - just traditional Vietnamese dishes - but very good. A great place to entertain wealthy foreign visitors.\n\nOwned by the same person who owns the overpriced coffee chain RuNam, so prices are high here too. He used to co-own the best Viet restaurant in Singapore, also called Nước, but unfortunately that closed down after a short period.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 30, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
